    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\nB0D5A8F7E7A61FABEF4565DF859E103B77CE08E26F70308561267EB89DAC8262FEE0ADD58CAC\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.2.\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n_No response_\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Qt Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Start a call with a user or group/conference\n3. Once the call starts, navigate to another part of the app such as a different user or channel, settings etc\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nAfter the reproduction steps, it is now impossible to know you are transmitting audio/video through the call, unless you happen to navigate back to the user/channel which the call is in. This is a fairly serious privacy risk in my opinion. Someone might do a call with someone, then forget to end the call, and have no way of knowing they are still transmitting audio and video unless they cycle through every single contact and conference they could possibly be in a call with.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThere should be some indication that a call is in progress, in the tray icon and/or in the app. An example is Discord which shows a panel in the bottom left when in a voice call or room.\n<img width=\"870\" height=\"276\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e32d5014-2175-4736-82c7-7051d36650c4\" />\n\nIdeally, this could have buttons to navigate to the user/conference the call is in, or end the call or mute/deafen.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nLinux Mint 22.1 Cinnamon\n\nEDIT: I realize this might actually count more as a feature request and a bug, sorry.. I started writing this under the assumption that it was a bug and forgot to change it before posting..",
